# {ProjectName} — Web-Novel Writing Toolkit

## Skill Routing Table

| Command | Skill | Description |
|------|-------|------|
| `/story-long-write`, write long-form | story-long-write | Long-form web-novel writing (chapter by chapter) |
| `/story-short-write`, write short-form | story-short-write | Short-form web-novel writing (emotion-driven) |
| `/story-long-analyze`, long-form teardown | story-long-analyze | Deep teardown of a long-form novel |
| `/story-short-analyze`, short-form teardown | story-short-analyze | Teardown analysis of a short-form novel |
| `/story-long-scan`, long-form scan | story-long-scan | Batch scanning of long-form novels |
| `/story-short-scan`, short-form scan | story-short-scan | Batch scanning of short-form novels |
| `/story-deslop`, de-AI-flavor | story-deslop | Removes AI writing traces |
| `/story-cover`, cover | story-cover | Generates cover images |
| `/story-review`, review | story-review | Multi-perspective adversarial review |
| `/story-import`, import | story-import | Reverse-imports an existing novel into the project structure |
| `/story`, web novels | story | Toolkit router · auto-routes ambiguous intent |
| `/story-setup`, prepare to write a book | story-setup | Environment deployment · one-click deployment of hooks/rules/agents |
| `/browser-cdp` | browser-cdp | Browser CDP tool |

## File Structure

- `teardown-lib/` — teardown analysis output directory
- `{BookTitle}/prose/` — long-form novel prose chapters
- `{BookTitle}/setting/` — character settings, world settings
- `{BookTitle}/outline/` — volume outlines, chapter outlines
- `{BookTitle}/tracking/` — context.md (writing context), foreshadowing.md
- `{BookTitle}/benchmark/` — benchmark-book analysis

## Collaboration Rules

Coordination between agents is defined by the responsibility boundaries in each agent definition file; no separate coordination-rule file is needed.

## Restoring Context After Compact

This section takes effect automatically after a compact. AGENTS.md is reloaded after every compact.
Key writing context:
1. Current writing project name and progress
2. Recently discussed character-setting changes
3. List of unresolved foreshadowing
4. The current chapter's emotion/rhythm targets

If {BookTitle}/tracking/context.md exists, read it first after a compact to restore context.
